[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"GameFramework Core: World, GameMode, GameState, PlayerController, and Pawn in Unreal Engine"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Understanding Unreal Engine's gameplay framework is crucial for building robust, scalable multiplayer and single-player games. At the heart of this architecture are five fundamental classes: UWorld, AGameMode, AGameState, APlayerController, and APawn. This tutorial explores the roles of these classes and how they interact."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. UWorld: The Container of Reality"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"UWorld is the top-level object that represents the collection of levels making up your game. It handles the spawning of actors, manages the physics simulation, and holds references to the persistent level, streaming levels, and the current GameMode and GameState."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"2. AGameMode: The Rules of Engagement"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"The GameMode class defines the game being played. It sets the rules, scoring, respawn conditions, and win states. Crucially, AGameMode only exists on the server in a multiplayer environment, meaning clients never have a direct reference to it. Use GameMode for authoritative logic."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"UCLASS()
class AMyGameMode : public AGameModeBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()
public:
    AMyGameMode();
    virtual void BeginPlay() override;
    virtual void Logout(AController* Exiting) override;
};"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"3. AGameState: The Shared State of the World"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"While GameMode is server-only, AGameState exists on both the server and all connected clients. Its job is to manage and replicate the state of the game to everyone. This includes match timers, player lists, team scores, and any global match progress variables."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"UCLASS()
class AMyGameState : public AGameStateBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()
public:
    UPROPERTY(ReplicatedUsing = OnRep_MatchTime, BlueprintReadOnly)
    float RemainingMatchTime;

    UFUNCTION()
    void OnRep_MatchTime();
};"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"4. APlayerController: The Mind of the Player"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The PlayerController is the interface between the human player and the pawn they are possessing in the world. It processes input, handles HUD creation, and manages camera views. In multiplayer, every client has exactly one local PlayerController, while the server has one PlayerController for every connected player."},{"order":13,"bullet_point":"Receives raw input from keyboards, mice, or gamepads."},{"order":14,"bullet_point":"Handles RPCs (Remote Procedure Calls) to communicate securely with the server."},{"order":15,"bullet_point":"Manages UI elements and HUD classes specific to that local user."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"5. APawn: The Physical Avatar"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"APawn is the base class for all actors that can be possessed by players or AI controllers. It represents the physical embodiment in the world. ACharacter is a specialized subclass of APawn designed specifically for bipedal movement, complete with a CharacterMovementComponent."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"void AMyPlayerController::SetupInputComponent()
{
    Super::SetupInputComponent();
    InputComponent->BindAxis("MoveForward", this, &AMyPlayerController::MoveForward);
}

void AMyPlayerController::MoveForward(float Value)
{
    if (APawn* ControlledPawn = GetPawn())
    {
        ControlledPawn->AddMovementInput(ControlledPawn->GetActorForwardVector(), Value);
    }
}"},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"Summary of the Architecture"},{"order":20,"bullet_point":"UWorld manages all actors and levels."},{"order":21,"bullet_point":"AGameMode dictates rules and runs exclusively on the server."},{"order":22,"bullet_point":"AGameState replicates overall game status to all clients."},{"order":23,"bullet_point":"APlayerController translates player input into actions."},{"order":24,"bullet_point":"APawn physically acts out those instructions in the UWorld."}]
